          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Self-leveling lasers use a pendulum or electronic sensors to find level automatically, which makes them faster and more consistent than manual lasers that rely on bubble vials. Manual or lock mode on a self-leveling laser remains valuable for stairs, slopes and angled layout, as long as you remember the line is no longer level.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people, a self-leveling laser with a lock mode is the right tool. Learn its warning signals, lock the pendulum when moving it, and check accuracy after any drop. Our <a href="/best-laser-level/">laser level buying guide</a> lists the models we recommend.
          </p>
